  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE 00\rE 01\rE 02\rE 03\rE 04\rP 00\rP 01\rP 02 \rP 03\rP 04\rP 05\rP 06\rP 07\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen / dining room and living room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the amenity of neighbours and the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved refuse storage details as set out in drawings P 01 and P 07 before the development is occupied. The refuse storage shall be retained and maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of refuse storage in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance 2024\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans, the development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of the provision of six long-stay cycle parking spaces within the front garden have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved facilities shall be installed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and thereafter retained for that purpose.\rThese details should demonstrate:\rLocation: within the front garden\rDesign: Stands or wall bars\rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit\rCoverage: Covered and secure\rAccessibility: Step-free, no obstructions\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first\roccupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r"
  ]
